This project downloads, invokes, or stages the following third-party
components at runtime; it does not redistribute them:

1. QEMU — a fast processor emulator (GPLv2) — fetched by
   scripts/fetch-qemu.ps1 from qemu.weilnetz.de
2. wimboot — iPXE Windows Imaging Format bootloader (GPLv2+) — fetched as
   the media bootloader; see https://ipxe.org/wimboot
3. wimlib — WIM compression library and tools (GPLv3 tools / LGPLv3
   library) — wimsplit is used to split install.wim under FAT32's 4 GiB
   per-file ceiling; see https://wimlib.net
4. EDK2 / OVMF / AAVMF UEFI firmware (BSD-2-Clause-Patent and others) —
   staged from Fedora's edk2-ovmf / edk2-aarch64 RPMs; the QEMU-bundled
   firmware is too old for Windows 24H2+ installation media
5. virtio-win drivers (GPLv2) — staged from Fedora's virtio-win feed for
   ARM64 guests (NIC/GPU drivers Windows ARM64 lacks in-box)
6. Windows ISOs — supplied by the user, or optionally auto-downloaded from
   NTDEV's tiny11 archive.org item. Windows itself is NOT open source; a
   valid Windows license remains the user's responsibility. FreshWin never
   redistributes Windows images.
